= Scope and objectives <sec:scope>

What this work sets out to do, and the boundary around it.

The three deliverables: a typed client for the instrument protocol, a framework
for writing SPM routines against it, and a tip-preparation routine built on
both. What "the routine worked" means concretely, so that @sec:validation can
be read as evidence rather than as description.

Out of scope, and deliberately so: tip functionalization, instrument backends
other than Nanonis, and the learned-policy work of @sec:outlook.
